    {
      "id": "M1h0QSHpR-7TXJLc21Mht",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1421.3673767711286,
      "y": 731.6146983046799,
      "width": 258.6797790527344,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2024701059,
      "version": 300,
      "versionNonce": 1453375779,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790186145254,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Can we extract the body?\n- try extract mechanically\n- write as no-body if can't",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Can we extract the body?\n- try extract mechanically\n- write as no-body if can't",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aLQCS1OMMm8IKwi2YSAn2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 688.0389628209272,
      "y": 1551.7031082672272,
      "width": 987.6169363492418,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b11",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 398986019,
      "version": 3456,
      "versionNonce": 1100541869,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790189047996,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Caveats and open questions:\n- arguably, we only intake articles that have bodies, because later it's not clear if we can process\nthe articles if the headline is not obvious\n    - in that case, do we mark articles without bodies as seen to filter them by URL in teh future?\n    - we may the article as no-body or headline-only\n    - the bet is if it's a really impotant news, it will reverberate through the outlefts where we can\nget body\n- embeddings over last X days for semantic dedup needs to be based on data of now long in the\npause between two articles in the same story can be (median, p80, p90?)\n- perhaps we should separate story and claim officially: claim is one happening/occasion, and story is\nan overarching plot of which several claims can be part of. For example: Donchenko/Soriano fight is\na story, and all the news inside are part of it like announcement, pre-fight analysis, predictions,\nweigh-ins, face-off, fight, results, post-fight interviews, post-fight analysis. Then, story may be a\nuseful aggregation for the digest writer, whily the system operate at the claim level. \n- also there seems emerge a question - what's a claim for different types of news. If extractor\nexperiment it became evident that most claims are occasions, while fight prediction articles are\ngrouped by type (prediction by each separate outselt/person is an occasion but they all are a single\nclaim because of noise - dozens of preductions). \n- All parts, especially Classifier, Extractor, Semantic dedup, and Decider\nneeds to be thoroughly tested in isolation.\n- should we update the claim as more articles arrive and add missing pieces to the claim? Does the\ndata support it? If we update, is the a risk claim will grow uncontrollably?\n- do we need a higher grade LLM for the digest writer? Does it need a web search?\n- does classifier route article for different types of extraction?\n- there needs to be a way to observe/diagnose all decisions teh pipeline makes and provide feedback\nfor future improvements.\n  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Caveats and open questions:\n- arguably, we only intake articles that have bodies, because later it's not clear if we can process the articles if the headline is not obvious\n    - in that case, do we mark articles without bodies as seen to filter them by URL in teh future?\n    - we may the article as no-body or headline-only\n    - the bet is if it's a really impotant news, it will reverberate through the outlefts where we can get body\n- embeddings over last X days for semantic dedup needs to be based on data of now long in the pause between two articles in the same story can be (median, p80, p90?)\n- perhaps we should separate story and claim officially: claim is one happening/occasion, and story is an overarching plot of which several claims can be part of. For example: Donchenko/Soriano fight is a story, and all the news inside are part of it like announcement, pre-fight analysis, predictions, weigh-ins, face-off, fight, results, post-fight interviews, post-fight analysis. Then, story may be a useful aggregation for the digest writer, whily the system operate at the claim level. \n- also there seems emerge a question - what's a claim for different types of news. If extractor experiment it became evident that most claims are occasions, while fight prediction articles are grouped by type (prediction by each separate outselt/person is an occasion but they all are a single claim because of noise - dozens of preductions). \n- All parts, especially Classifier, Extractor, Semantic dedup, and Decider\nneeds to be thoroughly tested in isolation.\n- should we update the claim as more articles arrive and add missing pieces to the claim? Does the data support it? If we update, is the a risk claim will grow uncontrollably?\n- do we need a higher grade LLM for the digest writer? Does it need a web search?\n- does classifier route article for different types of extraction?\n- there needs to be a way to observe/diagnose all decisions teh pipeline makes and provide feedback for future improvements.\n  ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
